# Line ending policy.
# Scripts and config files that end up inside Linux Docker images must keep LF:
# a CRLF shebang breaks the interpreter lookup (e.g. "./gradlew: not found", exit 127)
# during the image build, no matter what core.autocrlf the developer has locally.

* text=auto

gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
crontab text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.* text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

# Env files are read by docker compose and injected into containers as-is:
# a trailing CR turns a numeric value into a parse error on service startup.
.env* text eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.jar binary
*.lockb binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
